# React Conventions (easyCMDB)

## Components

- Function components only. No class components.
- One component per file for pages; shared components may co-locate small helpers.
- Typed props with `type XxxProps = { … }` — never `any`.
- Default export for route pages; named exports for reusable components when appropriate.
- Prefer explicit return types on exported functions and hooks.

## Hooks

- Follow Rules of Hooks — no conditional hook calls.
- Server/async data: TanStack Query (`useQuery`, `useMutation`) via `src/hooks/*`.
- Auth state: Zustand selectors from `@/stores/auth` — not React Context for session.
- UI-only state: `useState` / `useMemo` / `useCallback` locally.
- Side effects that touch auth or axios: wire in `main.tsx` or dedicated modules, not scattered in pages.

## Routing

- Import from `react-router` (v7 unified package), **not** `react-router-dom`.
- Use `createBrowserRouter`, `RouterProvider`, `Navigate`, `Outlet`, `useNavigate`, `useLocation`.
- Lazy-load page components with `React.lazy` + `<Suspense>` (see `router/index.tsx`).
- Preserve existing URL paths and route names during changes.

## Events & forms

- Controlled inputs for forms; validate before submit.
- `onSubmit` on `<form>` with `preventDefault` — avoid inline submit handlers without form semantics when a form exists.
- Async handlers: `async function handleX(): Promise<void>` with try/catch + `parseApiError`.

## JSX style

- Self-close void elements (`<input />`, `<img />`).
- `className` with Tailwind utilities; merge with `cn()` when conditional.
- No inline `style={{}}` unless dynamic values cannot be expressed in Tailwind.
- Keys on list items must be stable IDs, not array index (unless static reorder-free lists).

## Testing

- Use `@testing-library/react` patterns when adding component tests (Vitest + happy-dom).
- Colocate tests in `__tests__/` next to the module under test.
- Mock API modules, not axios globally, when testing pages.

## Avoid

- `any`, `as any`, non-null assertion (`!`) unless unavoidable (e.g. `document.getElementById`).
- Fetching in `useEffect` when a Query hook already exists for that resource.
- Duplicating auth logic outside `stores/auth.ts` and `router/index.tsx`.
- Importing from `react-router-dom` — the project uses `react-router`.
